From a03d003c9cc2c1dbb1d5ba3083faa2de378c756a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:43:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/65] Port Create New Character with its character-record
 helpers

Port H013+$0982 Create_Character from the assembly: race, gender,
class, god and alignment menus, starting levels and experience, age,
the stat rolls with age, race and class limits, hit points, gold and
the save prompt. Also port the local routines H013+$0524, $07B2,
$08C2, $0990 and $56CE, and the helpers they call: H053+$0012
(free a character), H062+$156C and $15F2 (dice, effects), H073+$09BA,
$0BA8, $0FC8 and $12C8 (cleric spells, saving throws, thief skills).

Add character.h: the $1AA-byte record keeps the original offsets, and
its pointer fields are separate members because host pointers are
eight bytes. The character sheet (H065), training (H013+$58DC), the
icon editor (H047) and saving (H066) are still unported stubs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
